    "q-104392": {
      "dom_id": "step-q104392",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following is **not** a set?",
      "worked_solution": "A set is a collection of elements listed between two braces (curly brackets). However, note that the null set (the set that does not contain any elements) can be written as either $\\{\\}$ or $∅.$\n\n- $\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}$ is *not* a set. The numbers $\\frac{2}{7},$ $\\frac{2}{5},$ $\\frac{2}{3},$ and $\\frac{1}{2}$ are *not* listed between two braces.\n\nAll the other choices are sets.\n\n- $\\{\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}\\}$ is a set. The elements are $\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}$ and they are listed between two braces.\n\n- $\\{\\{\\}\\}$ is a set. It contains a single element, $\\{\\},$ and this element is between two braces.\n\n- $\\{\\}$ is a set. It is the null set.\n\n- $∅$ is a set. It is the null set.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
